-- ccc21-part-19-absolute.l4 -- PART XIX, Indictable Offences -- Trial Without Jury: section 552 (the definition of "judge", for this Part) and section 553
-- (the offences over which a provincial court judge has absolute jurisdiction), of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Split from the rest of Part XIX because Part XVIII (ss 536, 536.1) asks section 553's answer and Part XIX (ss 554 and following) asks Part XVIII's: modules cannot import each other.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, each with a quoted `-- FALSE-kind` comment); NOTHING (not covered, each with a `-- NOTHING-kind` comment).

§ `PART XIX -- Section 552: Definitions`

-- 552 In this Part, judge means, (a) in the Province of Ontario, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province, (b) in Quebec, a judge of the Court of Quebec, ... (j) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
-- The kinds of office the paragraphs name. "judge means" is a closed definition.
-- src:12216 | judge means,
-- src:12217 | (a) in the Province of Ontario, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province,
-- src:12218 | (b) in the Province of Quebec, a judge of the Court of Quebec,
-- src:12219 | (c) in the Province of Nova Scotia, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province,
-- src:12220 | (d) in the Province of New Brunswick, a judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench,
-- src:12221 | (e) in the Province of British Columbia, the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Supreme Court,
-- src:12222 | (f) in the Province of Prince Edward Island, a judge of the Supreme Court,
-- src:12223 | (g) in the Province of Manitoba, the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench,
-- src:12224 | (h) in the Provinces of Saskatchewan and Alberta, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province,
-- src:12225 | (h.1) in the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, a judge of the Supreme Court,
-- src:12226 | (i) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of the Supreme Court, and
-- src:12227 | (j) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice. (juge)
@ref s 552 "judge" (src:12216-12227)
DECLARE `s 552 judge, who the person is` IS ONE OF
    `s 552 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province`   -- (a) Ontario, (c) Nova Scotia, (h) Saskatchewan and Alberta
    `s 552 a judge of the Court of Quebec`   -- (b)
    `s 552 a judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench`   -- (d) New Brunswick
    `s 552 the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Supreme Court`   -- (e) British Columbia
    `s 552 a judge of the Supreme Court`   -- (f) Prince Edward Island, (h.1) Newfoundland and Labrador, (i) Yukon and the Northwest Territories
    `s 552 the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench`   -- (g) Manitoba
    `s 552 a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`   -- (j)
    `s 552 a judicial officer who is none of those`

-- src:12216 | judge means,
-- src:12217 | (a) in the Province of Ontario, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province,
-- src:12218 | (b) in the Province of Quebec, a judge of the Court of Quebec,
-- src:12219 | (c) in the Province of Nova Scotia, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province,
-- src:12220 | (d) in the Province of New Brunswick, a judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench,
-- src:12221 | (e) in the Province of British Columbia, the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Supreme Court,
-- src:12222 | (f) in the Province of Prince Edward Island, a judge of the Supreme Court,
-- src:12223 | (g) in the Province of Manitoba, the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench,
-- src:12224 | (h) in the Provinces of Saskatchewan and Alberta, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province,
-- src:12225 | (h.1) in the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, a judge of the Supreme Court,
-- src:12226 | (i) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of the Supreme Court, and
-- src:12227 | (j) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice. (juge)
@ref s 552 "judge" (src:12216-12227)
GIVEN `the province or territory` IS A `Province or territory`
      `the person` IS A `s 552 judge, who the person is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 552 judge` MEANS
    IF `the person is named for the province or territory`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part, judge means"
    WHERE
        `the person is named for the province or territory` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the province or territory`
            WHEN Ontario THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province`
            WHEN Quebec THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the Court of Quebec`
            WHEN `Nova Scotia` THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province`
            WHEN `New Brunswick` THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench`
            WHEN `British Columbia` THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Supreme Court`
            WHEN `Prince Edward Island` THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the Supreme Court`
            WHEN Manitoba THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 the Chief Justice or a puisne judge of the Court of Queen’s Bench`
            WHEN Saskatchewan THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province`
            WHEN Alberta THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province`
            WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the Supreme Court`
            WHEN Yukon THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the Supreme Court`
            WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the Supreme Court`
            WHEN Nunavut THEN `the person` EQUALS `s 552 a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`

