§ `Section 553 -- Absolute jurisdiction`

-- 553 The jurisdiction of a provincial court judge, or in Nunavut, of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice, to try an accused is absolute and does not depend on the consent of the accused where the accused is charged in an information
-- (a) with (i) theft, other than theft of cattle, (ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences, (iii) unlawfully having in his possession ... (iv) having ... defrauded ... or (v) mischief under subsection 430(4),
-- where the subject-matter of the offence is not a testamentary instrument and the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence does not exceed five thousand dollars;
-- src:12234 | 553 The jurisdiction of a provincial court judge, or in Nunavut, of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice, to try an accused is absolute and does not depend on the consent of the accused where the accused is charged in an information
-- src:12235 | (a) with
-- src:12236 | (i) theft, other than theft of cattle,
-- src:12237 | (ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences,
-- src:12238 | (iii) unlawfully having in his possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or a part of the property or thing or of the proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment or an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment,
-- src:12239 | (iv) having, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means, defrauded the public or any person, whether ascertained or not, of any property, money or valuable security, or
-- src:12240 | (v) mischief under subsection 430(4),
-- src:12241 | where the subject-matter of the offence is not a testamentary instrument and the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence does not exceed five thousand dollars;
@ref s 553(a) (src:12234-12241)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 553 the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553(a) the offence charged is one paragraph (a) names, of a kind and value it covers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF charge's `s 553 the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` EQUALS `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) names five offences and says nothing of another
        IF charge's `s 553 the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` EQUALS `s 553(a)(i) theft` AND charge's `s 553 the theft is theft of cattle` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "theft, other than theft of cattle"
        IF charge's `s 553 the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the subject-matter of the offence is not a testamentary instrument"
        IF charge's `s 553 the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence does not exceed five thousand dollars"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 553 (b) with counselling or with a conspiracy or attempt to commit or with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of (i) any offence referred to in paragraph (a) in respect of the subject-matter and value thereof referred to in that paragraph, or (ii) any offence referred to in paragraph (c);
-- src:12242 | (b) with counselling or with a conspiracy or attempt to commit or with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of
-- src:12243 | (i) any offence referred to in paragraph (a) in respect of the subject-matter and value thereof referred to in that paragraph, or
-- src:12244 | (ii) any offence referred to in paragraph (c); or
@ref s 553(b) (src:12242-12244)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 553 the charge`
      `the answer of s 553(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 553(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553(b) the accused is charged with counselling, conspiracy, attempt or being an accessory after the fact to an offence in paragraph (a) or (c)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF charge's `s 553 how the accused is charged` EQUALS `s 553(b) with the offence itself` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with counselling or with a conspiracy or attempt to commit or with being an accessory after the fact"
        IF `the answer of s 553(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of s 553(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of s 553(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of the subject-matter and value thereof referred to in that paragraph"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any offence referred to in paragraph (a) in respect of the subject-matter and value thereof referred to in that paragraph, or (ii) any offence referred to in paragraph (c)"

