@ref s 553(c) (src:12245-12259)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 553 the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553(c) the accused is charged with an offence under a section paragraph (c) lists` MEANS
    IF    `the section` EQUALS 201 OR `the section` EQUALS 202 OR `the section` EQUALS 203 OR `the section` EQUALS 206 OR `the section` EQUALS 209
       OR `the section` EQUALS 393 OR `the section` EQUALS 490.031 OR `the section` EQUALS 490.0311 OR `the section` EQUALS 811
       OR (`the section` EQUALS 733.1 AND `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
       OR charge's `s 553 the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) names the sections it lists and says nothing of another
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS charge's `s 553 the offence charged`'s `section`
        `the subsection` MEANS charge's `s 553 the offence charged`'s `subsection`

