-- 553, taken whole: the jurisdiction of a provincial court judge (in Nunavut, of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice) to try the accused is absolute and does not depend on the consent of the accused
-- "where the accused is charged in an information" with an offence within (a), (b) or (c). A "where" gate on a grant: when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; NOTES.md group G2).
-- src:12234 | 553 The jurisdiction of a provincial court judge, or in Nunavut, of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice, to try an accused is absolute and does not depend on the consent of the accused where the accused is charged in an information
@ref s 553 (src:12234-12234)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 553 the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT charge's `s 553 the accused is charged in an information` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused is charged in an information"
        IF `limb (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused is charged in an information"
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `s 553(a) the offence charged is one paragraph (a) names, of a kind and value it covers` charge
        `limb (c)` MEANS `s 553(c) the accused is charged with an offence under a section paragraph (c) lists` charge
        `limb (b)` MEANS `s 553(b) the accused is charged with counselling, conspiracy, attempt or being an accessory after the fact to an offence in paragraph (a) or (c)` charge `limb (a)` `limb (c)`
